  "notes": "Block-13 fields in FORM-366 FIELDS were garbled OCR artifacts ('M•oof<ciore•', 'R•portobl•', 'to', 'IRIS'); only the second, coherent row (cause D, system IG, component MON, manufacturer A576, reportable Y) was retained. Official cause_code is D per FORM-366 FIELDS block_13, though the top-level cause_code/category field was listed as TBD/provisional -- category left as 'provisional' string per source since no discrete category label was given beyond 'D'. Previous Occurrences section (E) in the narrative was truncated/garbled ('safety system to become inoperable') with no LER number, plant, or title given, so no stub LER/SIMILAR_TO edge was created per Rule 9's requirement for the cited LER number. Component failure data listed under 'In-core Monitoring' (EIIS MON) manufactured by ABB Combustion Engineering (A576), model 2001731-102. WO and verification lapses modeled as two distinct FailureMode nodes per Rule 5, not merged despite both stemming from the same root cause theme."
